# 1. In:
# An integer representing a person's age entered by the user via input().

# 2. Process:
# Converts the user input into an integer.
# Uses an if-elif-else conditional structure to test which age range the number falls into.

# 3. Out:
# A specific message displayed on the terminal corresponding to the identified life stage/age group.

# 4. My ranges, my boundaries, my messages:
# - Range 1 (0 to 12): "Enfant - Enjoy the carefree childhood days!"
# - Range 2 (13 to 19): "Teen/Tween - Navigating the teenage years!"
# - Range 3 (20 to 39): "Young Adult - Building your career and personal life!"
# - Range 4 (40 to 99): "Middle Aged / Senior - Gaining wisdom and experience!"
# - Range 5 (100+): "Immortal - You have reached legendary age!"
# Exact Boundaries: 13, 20, 40, and 100.
# Boundary logic: Values exactly on a boundary belong to the higher category (e.g., exactly 13 is a Teen).

# Observation Comments for "CHECK IT YOURSELF":
# Boundary Tests for Threshold 20 (Young Adult cutoff):
# - Age 19: Output -> Teen/Tween (Landed where intended: lower range)
# - Age 20: Output -> Young Adult (Landed where intended: boundary value belongs to upper range)
# - Age 21: Output -> Young Adult (Landed where intended: upper range)

# Your code below

age_input = input("Enter your age: ")
age = int(age_input)

# Check ranges using if-elif-else logic
if age < 0:
    print("Invalid age entered. Age cannot be negative.")
elif age < 13:
    print("Enfant - Enjoy the carefree childhood days!")
elif age < 20: # Covers ages 13 to 19
    print("Teen/Tween - Navigating the teenage years!")
elif age < 40: # Covers ages 20 to 39
    print("Young Adult - Building your career and personal life!")
elif age < 100: # Covers ages 40 to 99
    print("Middle Aged / Senior - Gaining wisdom and experience!")
else: # 100 and above
    print("Immortal - You have reached legendary age!")